t."] [65 1 "// ImageFresh reports whether out is the image of file as it is now."] [91 1 "// ---- the writer ----"] [99 1 "// strTab is an image's string table: the module's part and the code's share it."] [122 1 "// the literal values' tags"] [192 1 "// the nodes' tags"] [206 11 "// a tuple's worker as a constructor (unused)"] [330 1 "// encodeModule is the image of a module's forms."] [344 2 "// a loader of its own: names and constructors are records, nothing is loaded or run"] [441 2 "// the file: header, string table, module, code"] [456 1 "// closure writes a top-level closure's compiled code, or the error compiling it gives (raised when entered)."] [493 1 "// ---- the reader ----"] [703 1 "// imgSpan is a top-level closure's code in its module's image."] [706 1 "// loadImage loads a module from its image (as loadForms from its forms)."] [737 2 "// phase 0: the binders (strings, then bindings: their order in the image)"] [750 2 "// the bindings, read once: closures made at once, constructors' atoms after every binder is known"] [787 2 "// phase 1: the objects"] [814 2 "// phase 2: the constructors' fields"] [825 1 "// atom0 skips an atom (its literal's string literal not made)."] [842 1 "// reg registers a top-level binder of the module."] [852 1 "// compileImage decodes a top-level closure's code from its module's image."] [867 1 "// imgStrs is the image's string table (read again: the module keeps only the bytes)."] [882 1 "// imagePath is a module's image under the image directory, or \"\" when there is none or it is stale."] [891 1 "// SetImageDir makes the machine load the libraries' modules from their images in dir when they are fresh."] [894 1 "// Images is the number of modules loaded from their images."] [897 1 "// BuildImages writes the image of every module of the units in libs (as the loader finds them) that has no fresh"] [898 1 "// one under out, jobs at a time: the images made, those already fresh, the errors."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 